h respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =p(-1)q(-1)+p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2) \\\\  & =(2-k)(-1-1)+(2+k)(1-1)+(2+2k)(2-4) \\\\  & =(-4+2k)+0+(-4-4k) \\\\  & =-8-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨p(t),q(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ -8-2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-8 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97362/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a348cfec-2c8f-5302-a94a-43a6c9330c34"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97362"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" :answer/id #uuid "433b1c9b-5e99-5fa0-9151-7402fda71c6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer/id #uuid "e686df33-435a-5683-9189-72d7d4adee76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "b44b2bfe-94a6-5dce-af82-f2c4d2782d59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439/selection/f003b95a6c7a22f536ec799844670c061a2d01da9486469d5da5d96020e58645" :answer/id #uuid "9d4035ce-7e08-54c4-ab71-ef5115a511fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" :answer/id #uuid "8a02e2cc-c429-5bc2-ac92-43ac33cd11d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5682680-cce4-5e46-a5ae-a70fda8a4d19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97439/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d" :answer-field/choices ["q-97439/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" "q-97439/selection/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" "q-97439/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-97439/selection/f003b95a6c7a22f536ec799844670c061a2d01da9486469d5da5d96020e58645" "q-97439/selection/6bc991249a374b862f397b8c857af2e7218904b9402c1810129647c55070a69d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97439" :question/id #uuid "8ef93a42-95d6-5c7b-a187-5da2bd8f1e80" :question/math-academy-id "q-97439" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIf $x(t)={e}^{{t}^{2}}+k$ and $y(t)=t$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{{t}^{2}}+k)t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(t{e}^{{t}^{2}}+kt)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{{t}^{2}}}{2}+\\frac{k{t}^{2}}{2}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{e+k-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\frac{e+k-1}{2} & =0 \\\\ e+k-1 & =0 \\\\ k & =1-e\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97439/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "404853dd-2cdf-5ee0-b081-ebd6b8a90ee7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97439"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "12010cba-f248-5d6a-8810-51fc472e7ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7a6c9cdd-aea7-5136-98dd-821a993dde5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "33d28332-6d03-58b4-a539-b134af21347c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "3d5035b8-75a6-5f6e-a545-2e8030a10491" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "7b0c843d-90d5-56fc-9315-e9d561e95468" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "439fbe01-aa07-580c-b35c-46beccac224d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97436/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-97436/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-97436/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-97436/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-97436/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-97436/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97436" :question/id #uuid "f352e2be-b676-5530-8fa9-0bd1cab2042e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97436" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIf $x(t)=t-2{t}^{2}$ and $y(t)=t+k$ are orthogonal with respect to the inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ in $V,$ then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-2{t}^{2})(t+k)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(kt+(1-2k){t}^{2}-2{t}^{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{k{t}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(1-2k){t}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-1}{2}+\\frac{1-2k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\frac{k-1}{2}+\\frac{1-2k}{3} & =0 \\\\ 3(k-1)+2(1-2k) & =0 \\\\ 3k-3+2-4k & =0 \\\\ -1-k & =0 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97436/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "404853dd-2cdf-5ee0-b081-ebd6b8a90ee7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97436"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-44093/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "eea26417-b2c6-5e2e-8f81-64142aa6dedd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-44093/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3aeac1f8-35bb-577c-a673-b0d560acd939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4409